# std/hello's image: build this directory as a Rust project with rustc.
# `--src:@=.` hands rustc the tool (Cargo.toml + src/; rustc skips the caos
# metadata — .caos-expr, DEPS, DEEP-DEPS/), named by a LOCAL deep-deps mount
# declared in DEPS. No runner is named: rustc DEPENDS on the pool and curries
# the built binary onto it itself, so the result is
# curry(runner, worker1=<the compiled binary>).
run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=.
